CANTO II: “Is High Literature Dead?” (January 9, 2025)

1.

Even when I wasn’t famous, I dreamed of how I’d share my privileges and honor my love of literature after I became famous.

It’d be my honor to mentor you, since I thank God for your existence. It’s about keeping the craft alive.

I didn’t have any mentors.

Which makes me want to be a mentor even fucking more.

2.

We’re not cooks, no.

But I can teach you how to see your writing instrument as a chef’s knife; your room as your kitchen.

Maybe I can’t teach you anything.

But your wit is your spice. Your humor is your seasoning. Your insights are calories. Your syllables aren’t to be wasted.

3.

